RULES.md
verify
# Working notes, not configuration: the motion specification, the reference
# readings and the notes on the package lists. They stay where they were
# -~/.config and packages/-, but they do not come back into the repo.
home/.config/motion-language.md
home/.config/motion-language.en.md
home/.config/motion-referencias.md
home/.config/motion-references.en.md
packages/NOTES.md
# And the general rule, for the next notebook that gets written: a loose .md
# at the root of ~/.config is never configuration, it is notes. The READMEs
# that ARE versioned live inside their component's directory
# (quickshell/README.md), so this pattern does not touch them.
home/.config/*.md
# What was adapted from other projects is credited in the HEADER of each file,
# which is where the GPL wants it and where it does not get lost. The
# notebooks that discuss it on top of that are working notes, not
# configuration.
home/.config/quickshell/IMPASTO.md
home/.claude/
home/.codex/
home/.copilot/
home/.gemini/
home/.mcp.json
home/.agent-memory/
